<title>USA: U.S. October PPI energy goods prices.</title>
<headline>U.S. October PPI energy goods prices.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-11-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.S. Labor Department</p>
<p>reported energy components of the producer price index as follows, with comparisons (1982=100 unless stated otherwise).</p>
<p>    Percent Changes:   Seasonally Adj.  Unadjusted</p>
<p> -				 Oct   Sept    Oct96/95</p>
<p> Finished Energy Goods     1.9    0.2     9.5</p>
<p> -Gasoline		     5.5    0.9    21.7</p>
<p> -Heating Oil		  3.8    2.0    41.9</p>
<p> -Residential Gas-Y	 UNCH   -2.1     6.4</p>
<p>Y-Dec 1990=100.  </p>
<p>    Percent Changes:   Seasonally Adj.  Unadjusted</p>
<p> -				 Oct   Sept    Oct96/95</p>
<p> Intermed.Energy Goods     1.7    0.8    10.3</p>
<p> -Liq.Petroleum Gas-Z	18.4   0.1    43.8</p>
<p> -Jet Fuel		     1.6    6.8    33.3</p>
<p> -Diesel Fuel		  1.5    0.4    36.6</p>
<p> -Residual Fuel-Z	    3.4    0.2    34.8</p>
<p>Z-Current data not seasonally adjusted.  </p>
<p>    Percent Changes:   Seasonally Adj.  Unadjusted</p>
<p> -				 Oct    Sept   Oct96/95</p>
<p> Crude Energy Materials-Y  1.5    0.6    23.6</p>
<p> -Coal-Z			-2.5    3.1    -2.4</p>
<p> -Nat.Gas to Pipelines-Z  -3.2   -6.4    18.6</p>
<p> -Petroleum-Z		  8.5    7.3    48.4</p>
<p>Y-Includes crude petroleum. Z-Current data not seasonally adjusted.</p>
</text>
